<title>ITALY: Italian GDP rose 0.7 pct yr/yr in Q2 96.</title>
<headline>Italian GDP rose 0.7 pct yr/yr in Q2 96.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's gross domestic product (GDP) rose by a real 0.7 percent, year on year, in the second quarter of 1996, National Statistics Institute Istat said.</p>
<p> ITALIAN GDP			 Q2 1996  Q1 1996     Q2 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr growth (pct)		   +0.7  +1.3 (+1.5) +2.8 (+2.7)</p>
<p> Growth versus previous quarter   -0.4  +0.4 (+0.5) +0.2 (+0.1)</p>
<p> Overall value (trln lire)	 347.89   349.31     345.47</p>
<p>Note: - Figures in brackets denote orginally given data.  </p>
<p>Istat gave the following breakdown:</p>
<p> FINAL CONSUMPTION		  Q2 1996   Q1 1996    Q2 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr growth (pct)		 +0.2    +0.6 (+0.8)   +1.2</p>
<p> Growth versus previous quarter +0.1     0.0 (+0.1) +0.5 (+0.4)</p>
<p> Overall value (trln lire)	271.73    271.45	271.07</p>
<p> FIXED INVESTMENTS		  Q2 1996   Q1 1996    Q2 1995</p>
<p> Yr/yr growth (pct)		 +2.5    +3.6 (+3.8)  +5.7 (+5.8)</p>
<p> Growth versus previous quarter +0.6    -0.6 (-0.4)  +1.8</p>
<p> Overall value (trln lire)     62.14	61.76	60.66</p>
<p> STOCK VARIATIONS		   Q2 96    Q1 96     Q2 95</p>
<p> Yr/yr growth (pct)		   N/A     N/A	 N/A</p>
<p> Growth versus previous quarter   N/A     N/A	 N/A</p>
<p> Overall value (trln lire)	-1.39  +5.38 (4.68) 6.72 (-1.40)</p>
<p> EXPORTS OF GOODS AND SERVICES  Q2 96     Q1 96	 Q2 95</p>
<p> Yr/yr growth (pct)		 -2.7   +1.2 (+1.3) +16.9 (+17.2)</p>
<p> Growth versus previous quarter -0.5   +0.2 (+0.7)  +3.5  (+4.2)</p>
<p> Overall value (trln lire)	84.73     85.15	 87.06</p>
<p> IMPORTS OF GOODS AND SERVICES  Q2 96     Q1 96	 Q2 95</p>
<p> Yr/yr growth (pct)		 -4.7   +4.3 (+3.2) +11.0 (+12.7)</p>
<p> Growth versus previous quarter -5.2   -1.7 (-0.7)  +3.8 (+2.2)</p>
<p> Overall value (trln lire)	70.57     74.76	 68.15</p>
<p>Note: Istat has rebased its 1995 index on 1990 levels, replacing a 1985-based index. 1996 data was already based on 1990 levels.</p>
<p>Provisional second quarter data released in August showed GDP rising 0.5 percent year-on-year and falling 0.5 percent quarter-on-quarter. - Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
